ry of sexual violence  perhaps i'm not as confident in myself  because of my history you think he knew  that  yeah you think he was grooming you yeah  and bennett says on june 5th governor  cuomo crossed a line  he wanted a girlfriend when he said he  was lonely i mentioned that his  daughters had been around  and he also rejected that and said  yeah love my i love my daughters but  that's  i want a girlfriend bennett says he  asked whether she'd ever been with an  older man  what were you thinking as he's asking  you  these questions i thought he's trying to  sleep with me  the governor is trying to sleep with me  and  i'm deeply uncomfortable  and i have to get out of this room as  soon as possible and to be clear  what made you think that he was trying  to sleep with you without explicitly  saying it  he he implied  to me that i was old enough for him and  he was lonely  as you left work on june 5th  what were you thinking  i was trying not to cry i assumed  that i could no longer work for him i  gotta get out of this job  i'm not doing that again i'm not  engaging in that conversation or any  other conversation  i'm not putting myself in a position  where he physically comes onto me  it stops here that's it  but then you get called back into the  office the next day  saturday june 6th and you've never  talked about this before  no bennett says at one point on that  saturday  she was the only employee working with  the governor in his private office  i was terrified i was shaking  i i thought any moment something can  happen  and i have no power here and what  happens when you're with the governor  he asked me a few questions about how to  use his iphone  and then sends me back to wait and then  finally he calls me in and he  asks if i found him a girlfriend yet  he asked you again yes i say not yet  i said i was working on it governor  cuomo said in a statement  on sunday that he was just being playful  was it playful no  he says he was joking i wasn't laughing 